. *****************************************************************************
> ***
.  /*  H3: Having daughters leads to more gender equality within the household.
>   */
. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. 
. * Authors: [REDACTED], [REDACTED] (based on example code)
. 
. use "$DATA/h3_dataset.dta", clear

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 *
. 
.         /* We regress the Gini of nonpaid work in the household (measured in 
>         the year after the first child was born) on the first child being a g
> irl, 
>         age of the father and survey year. The Gini of nonpaid work is calcul
> ated 
>         as the absolute difference between the amount of nonpaid work (childc
> are, 
>         errands, repairs, housework, caring for persons) in a week by
>         the mother and the father, divided by the total nonpaid work. 0 means
>  total
>         equality, 1 means total inequality. */
. 
.         reg nonpaid_gini i.first_daughter father_age i.syear

      Source |       SS           df       MS      Number of obs   =        43
-------------+----------------------------------   F(12, 30)       =      1.67
       Model |  .875212307        12  .072934359   Prob > F        =    0.1245
    Residual |  1.30964613        30  .043654871   R-squared       =    0.4006
-------------+----------------------------------   Adj R-squared   =    0.1608
       Total |  2.18485844        42  .052020439   Root MSE        =    .20894

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
nonpaid_gini | Coefficient  Std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
1.first_da~r |  -.1105635   .0781983    -1.41   0.168    -.2702657    .0491388
  father_age |  -.0073521   .0076612    -0.96   0.345    -.0229984    .0082941
             |
       syear |
       2003  |  -.2730438   .1708952    -1.60   0.121    -.6220584    .0759708
       2005  |  -.4490896   .1805079    -2.49   0.019     -.817736   -.0804432
       2007  |  -.2810187   .1164633    -2.41   0.022    -.5188686   -.0431689
       2009  |  -.2574603   .1730574    -1.49   0.147    -.6108907    .0959701
       2011  |  -.2251947   .1054412    -2.14   0.041    -.4405343    -.009855
       2012  |  -.7050145   .2298759    -3.07   0.005    -1.174484   -.2355453
       2013  |  -.0953727   .1325765    -0.72   0.477      -.36613    .1753847
       2015  |  -.3992562   .1782895    -2.24   0.033     -.763372   -.0351404
       2017  |     -.1932   .1733892    -1.11   0.274     -.547308    .1609079
       2019  |  -.1747435   .1234692    -1.42   0.167    -.4269012    .0774142
             |
       _cons |   1.021437   .2908604     3.51   0.001      .427421    1.615454
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[1.first_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[1.first_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[1.first_daughter] / _se[1.first_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 local interpretation "negative coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
.         // Display the saved statistics
